Maintainer: Aryan Kamal <aryan.kamal@unibas.ch>
Description: Provides methods to estimate transcriptional entropy for
    individual cells in Seurat objects and AnnData h5ad files. It supports
    BUB-based and binary entropy estimation using neighborhood gene expression,
    with direct integration into R, Seurat, Python, and Scanpy workflows.
    Optional count-depth correction thins every cell to a common library
    depth before estimation, because sequencing depth inflates entropy for
    purely technical reasons. A restartable depth-selection sweep chooses a
    correction quantile by balancing removed depth-aligned variance against
    retained variation. An interventional check can also alter an input and
    recompute entropy to ask whether a cluster ranking survives.
